			<title>FPL Friday - time to replace Reece James?</title>
			<itunes:title>FPL Friday - time to replace Reece James?</itunes:title>
			<pubDate>Fri, 29 Apr 2022 15:42:32 GMT</pubDate>
			<itunes:duration>20:53</itunes:duration>
			<enclosure url="https://sphinx.acast.com/p/open/s/683750c96e5b65d787575771/e/bd5867cc-ac4d-11ec-9930-13e2f0775c80/media.mp3" length="30112993" type="audio/mpeg"/>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">bd5867cc-ac4d-11ec-9930-13e2f0775c80</guid>
			<itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
			<link>https://theathletic.com/podcast/166-fpl-podcast/?episode=108</link>
			<acast:episodeId>683750e57b483718e05ed13c</acast:episodeId>
			<acast:showId>683750c96e5b65d787575771</acast:showId>
			<acast:settings><![CDATA[]]></acast:settings>
			<itunes:subtitle><![CDATA[FPL General is here ahead of Saturday's gameweek 34 deadline with some last minute advice to help you push on record a strong end to the FPL season as we enter the closings stages.]]></itunes:subtitle>
			<itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
			<itunes:image href="https://assets.pippa.io/shows/683750c96e5b65d787575771/show-cover.jpg"/>
			<description><![CDATA[FPL General is here ahead of Saturday's gameweek 35 deadline with some last minute advice to help you push on record a strong end to the FPL season as we enter the closings stages.</p><ul><li>Do I sell James for Cancelo?</li><li>Replace Reece James with Laporte or Alonso and is Matty Cash a good buy for upcoming fixtures?</li><li>Which Chelsea players are most likely to be rotated against Everton? Worth selling Werner and Havertz/Mount for Watkins and Coutinho?</li><li>Is Ramsey a good Villa asset to bring in to attack their upcoming fixtures, if you're tight on funds? Him or Dewsbury-Hall as a cheap midfielder?</li><li>Who is the better buy for the rest of the season... Foden or Coutinho? Or, hold Havertz and re-evaluate next week with two FT's before the double?</li><li>Sell Sterling for Son or go without Spurs players for the run-in?</li><li>Is a triple up on Arsenal attackers a viable option with the players being Saka, Odegaard and Nketiah?</li><li>Would you consider Zaha? Playing the worst defence in Southampton next followed by another poor defence in Watford followed by a decent double in 37?</li><li>Best Broja replacements? Need a striker for bench boost on DGW36?</li><li>Would it be safe to double up on Man City and Liverpool defenders?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></description>
			<itunes:summary><![CDATA[FPL General is here ahead of Saturday's gameweek 35 deadline with some last minute advice to help you push on record a strong end to the FPL season as we enter the closings stages.</p><ul><li>Do I sell James for Cancelo?</li><li>Replace Reece James with Laporte or Alonso and is Matty Cash a good buy for upcoming fixtures?</li><li>Which Chelsea players are most likely to be rotated against Everton? Worth selling Werner and Havertz/Mount for Watkins and Coutinho?</li><li>Is Ramsey a good Villa asset to bring in to attack their upcoming fixtures, if you're tight on funds? Him or Dewsbury-Hall as a cheap midfielder?</li><li>Who is the better buy for the rest of the season... Foden or Coutinho? Or, hold Havertz and re-evaluate next week with two FT's before the double?</li><li>Sell Sterling for Son or go without Spurs players for the run-in?</li><li>Is a triple up on Arsenal attackers a viable option with the players being Saka, Odegaard and Nketiah?</li><li>Would you consider Zaha? Playing the worst defence in Southampton next followed by another poor defence in Watford followed by a decent double in 37?</li><li>Best Broja replacements? Need a striker for bench boost on DGW36?</li><li>Would it be safe to double up on Man City and Liverpool defenders?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></itunes:summary>
