		<item>
			<title>Team news and transfer advice</title>
			<itunes:title>Team news and transfer advice</itunes:title>
			<pubDate>Fri, 01 Apr 2022 15:50:14 GMT</pubDate>
			<itunes:duration>19:00</itunes:duration>
			<enclosure url="https://sphinx.acast.com/p/open/s/683750c96e5b65d787575771/e/7aad440c-b1d3-11ec-b993-a3df30213f31/media.mp3" length="27409735" type="audio/mpeg"/>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">7aad440c-b1d3-11ec-b993-a3df30213f31</guid>
			<itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
			<link>https://theathletic.com/podcast/166-fpl-podcast/?episode=103</link>
			<acast:episodeId>683750e9998551779fb873d1</acast:episodeId>
			<acast:showId>683750c96e5b65d787575771</acast:showId>
			<acast:settings><![CDATA[]]></acast:settings>
			<itunes:subtitle>FPL General is here with a last-minute preview of gameweek 31 including some up-to-date team news and plenty of transfer advice</itunes:subtitle>
			<itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
			<itunes:image href="https://assets.pippa.io/shows/683750c96e5b65d787575771/show-cover.jpg"/>
			<description><![CDATA[FPL General is here with a last-minute preview of gameweek 31 including some up-to-date team news and plenty of transfer advice via answers to these questions:</p><ul><li>If we get the news that Trent Alexander-Arnold is not going to play against Watford, is it worth it to transfer him out? Then for who?</li><li>Which Chelsea defender to buy? James, Rudiger, Silva or Chalobah?</li><li>How much of a risk is bringing in Cancelo with an impending UCL fixture that Walker is suspended for?</li><li>Best Ramsdale replacement?</li><li>What to do with Coutinho? Put money in defence or get a Man City or Chelsea midfielder? </li><li>Havertz vs Foden vs Mahrez. Best long term hold? </li><li>Best strikers around the £5-6 million range?</li><li>Who are the must-have players on a GW31 wildcard?</li><li>I’m planning to free hit in GW33 and wildcard in GW34. With 2 frees I can punt on a player or two for GW31 and GW32, who would you suggest? </li><li>Is going with two non-playing bench players too risky if we are loading up on players from the likes of City and Chelsea?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></description>
			<itunes:summary><![CDATA[FPL General is here with a last-minute preview of gameweek 31 including some up-to-date team news and plenty of transfer advice via answers to these questions:</p><ul><li>If we get the news that Trent Alexander-Arnold is not going to play against Watford, is it worth it to transfer him out? Then for who?</li><li>Which Chelsea defender to buy? James, Rudiger, Silva or Chalobah?</li><li>How much of a risk is bringing in Cancelo with an impending UCL fixture that Walker is suspended for?</li><li>Best Ramsdale replacement?</li><li>What to do with Coutinho? Put money in defence or get a Man City or Chelsea midfielder? </li><li>Havertz vs Foden vs Mahrez. Best long term hold? </li><li>Best strikers around the £5-6 million range?</li><li>Who are the must-have players on a GW31 wildcard?</li><li>I’m planning to free hit in GW33 and wildcard in GW34. With 2 frees I can punt on a player or two for GW31 and GW32, who would you suggest? </li><li>Is going with two non-playing bench players too risky if we are loading up on players from the likes of City and Chelsea?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></itunes:summary>
