			<acast:episodeId>683750ec9bd0275f2c4a45f2</acast:episodeId>
			<acast:showId>683750c96e5b65d787575771</acast:showId>
			<acast:settings><![CDATA[]]></acast:settings>
			<itunes:subtitle>FPL General is here to get you back focused on your FPL team as we approach the end of the international break. He looks ahead to double gameweek 31 with his usual variety of advice on captaincy, transfers and players to add to the watchlist,</itunes:subtitle>
			<itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
			<itunes:image href="https://assets.pippa.io/shows/683750c96e5b65d787575771/show-cover.jpg"/>
			<description><![CDATA[FPL General is here to get you back focused on your FPL team as we approach the end of the international break. He looks ahead to double gameweek 31 with his usual variety of advice on captaincy, transfers, players to add to the watchlist, plus answers for these questions:</p><ul><li>Which Burnley assets (if any) would you be interested in bringing in for their DGW31 and future fixtures?</li><li> What are your thoughts on having NO DGW players for this week?</li><li> Is punting on Weghorst a good move?</li><li> Thoughts on picking five defenders from Liverpool, City and Chelsea?</li><li> Top 3 Man City assets and Top 3 Chelsea assets for the run-in?</li><li> Is it time to sell Raphinha for a Leicester midfielder?</li><li> Smith-Rowe to Saka for a hit?</li><li> What do you think of Man United assets, particularly given DGW33. Would a FH in GW33 eliminate any need for Man United assets?</li><li> With Ramsdale and Dubravka both in doubt, is Pope for a -4 a clever shout for GW31, given his doubles?</li><li> For those with 1 FH left, which do you think of FH33 or FH36 is better?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></description>
			<itunes:summary><![CDATA[FPL General is here to get you back focused on your FPL team as we approach the end of the international break. He looks ahead to double gameweek 31 with his usual variety of advice on captaincy, transfers, players to add to the watchlist, plus answers for these questions:</p><ul><li>Which Burnley assets (if any) would you be interested in bringing in for their DGW31 and future fixtures?</li><li> What are your thoughts on having NO DGW players for this week?</li><li> Is punting on Weghorst a good move?</li><li> Thoughts on picking five defenders from Liverpool, City and Chelsea?</li><li> Top 3 Man City assets and Top 3 Chelsea assets for the run-in?</li><li> Is it time to sell Raphinha for a Leicester midfielder?</li><li> Smith-Rowe to Saka for a hit?</li><li> What do you think of Man United assets, particularly given DGW33. Would a FH in GW33 eliminate any need for Man United assets?</li><li> With Ramsdale and Dubravka both in doubt, is Pope for a -4 a clever shout for GW31, given his doubles?</li><li> For those with 1 FH left, which do you think of FH33 or FH36 is better?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></itunes:summary>
