		<item>
			<title>Is this the week to triple captain Salah?</title>
			<itunes:title>Is this the week to triple captain Salah?</itunes:title>
			<pubDate>Tue, 15 Feb 2022 14:56:00 GMT</pubDate>
			<itunes:duration>28:33</itunes:duration>
			<enclosure url="https://sphinx.acast.com/p/open/s/683750c96e5b65d787575771/e/83e76ff2-8046-11ec-a255-2f5e6d69673d/media.mp3" length="41172755" type="audio/mpeg"/>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">83e76ff2-8046-11ec-a255-2f5e6d69673d</guid>
			<itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
			<link>https://theathletic.com/podcast/166-fpl-podcast/?episode=97</link>
			<acast:episodeId>683750ea998551779fb87522</acast:episodeId>
			<acast:showId>683750c96e5b65d787575771</acast:showId>
			<acast:settings><![CDATA[]]></acast:settings>
			<itunes:subtitle><![CDATA[FPL General reflects on gameweek 25 and casts his eyes upon the upcoming double gameweek 26 - with a host of teams playing twice it's another chance to rack up big points.]]></itunes:subtitle>
			<itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
			<itunes:image href="https://assets.pippa.io/shows/683750c96e5b65d787575771/show-cover.jpg"/>
			<description><![CDATA[FPL General reflects on gameweek 25 and casts his eyes upon the upcoming double gameweek 26 - with a host of teams playing twice it's another chance to rack up big points. There's transfer advice, captaincy picks, a watchlist update, plus these questions answered:</p><ul><li>Is Salah triple captain still on this week after his slight dip in form following the African Cup of Nations?</li><li> For those with Trent, Robertson &amp; Jota, which one would be best to lose to accommodate Salah?</li><li> If you have more than 4 fixtures being played by your bench players in Gw26, is boosting a preferable chip to TC? <strong> </strong></li><li> Who would your top 3 Arsenal assets be and why?</li><li> What should we do with Ronaldo?</li><li> Best 3 strikers to navigate GW26 &amp; 27 and beyond if not using a FH until GW30?</li><li> Kane or Son or neither for the DGW?</li><li> Who are the best 3 single GW options for the upcoming DGW26?</li><li> Which Wolves defender/(s) would you target on a DGW26 Free Hit?</li><li> Is it ok to bench Man City assets?</li><li> Do we stick with Raphina given his benching and tough fixtures or move to someone like Saka?</li><li> Which Burnley defender do you think is best as a punt for their two DGWs?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></description>
			<itunes:summary><![CDATA[FPL General reflects on gameweek 25 and casts his eyes upon the upcoming double gameweek 26 - with a host of teams playing twice it's another chance to rack up big points. There's transfer advice, captaincy picks, a watchlist update, plus these questions answered:</p><ul><li>Is Salah triple captain still on this week after his slight dip in form following the African Cup of Nations?</li><li> For those with Trent, Robertson &amp; Jota, which one would be best to lose to accommodate Salah?</li><li> If you have more than 4 fixtures being played by your bench players in Gw26, is boosting a preferable chip to TC? <strong> </strong></li><li> Who would your top 3 Arsenal assets be and why?</li><li> What should we do with Ronaldo?</li><li> Best 3 strikers to navigate GW26 &amp; 27 and beyond if not using a FH until GW30?</li><li> Kane or Son or neither for the DGW?</li><li> Who are the best 3 single GW options for the upcoming DGW26?</li><li> Which Wolves defender/(s) would you target on a DGW26 Free Hit?</li><li> Is it ok to bench Man City assets?</li><li> Do we stick with Raphina given his benching and tough fixtures or move to someone like Saka?</li><li> Which Burnley defender do you think is best as a punt for their two DGWs?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></itunes:summary>
