		<item>
			<title>Do we get Salah straight back in?</title>
			<itunes:title>Do we get Salah straight back in?</itunes:title>
			<pubDate>Fri, 11 Feb 2022 14:50:00 GMT</pubDate>
			<itunes:duration>29:57</itunes:duration>
			<enclosure url="https://sphinx.acast.com/p/open/s/683750c96e5b65d787575771/e/83fb2312-8046-11ec-a255-cbf1048ffdea/media.mp3" length="43182113" type="audio/mpeg"/>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">83fb2312-8046-11ec-a255-cbf1048ffdea</guid>
			<itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
			<link>https://theathletic.com/podcast/166-fpl-podcast/?episode=96</link>
			<acast:episodeId>683750de998551779fb87109</acast:episodeId>
			<acast:showId>683750c96e5b65d787575771</acast:showId>
			<acast:settings><![CDATA[]]></acast:settings>
			<itunes:subtitle><![CDATA[The midweek fixtures are in the books so FPL General is here to preview gameweek 25 with a tight turnaround to Saturday's 11am deadline.]]></itunes:subtitle>
			<itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
			<itunes:image href="https://assets.pippa.io/shows/683750c96e5b65d787575771/show-cover.jpg"/>
			<description><![CDATA[The midweek fixtures are in the books so FPL General is here to preview gameweek 25 with a tight turnaround to Saturday's 11am deadline. All the usual wisdom plus these questions answered:</p><ul><li>Is it worth buying Bruno for the DGW or going straight to Salah?</li><li>Thoughts on bench boost in GW26 over TC Salah?</li><li>Is this a good time to wildcard without having Salah and a few players I’m not happy with?</li><li>What’s the plan to bring Salah back if I have KDB and Bruno?</li><li>Weghorst or Cornet to target for Burnley's double double?</li><li>Is Antonio to Weghorst the best move?</li><li>Should we replace Foden with Coutinho and is Dalot a good option going forward as a 5th defender?</li><li>What do you think about Raphinha, Watkins &amp; Antonio?</li><li>Which five players should we be targeting for DGW26?</li><li>Edouard benched again. Should we admit we got it wrong and cut our losses? Or hold for the good run fixtures and have faith that he’ll return?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></description>
			<itunes:summary><![CDATA[The midweek fixtures are in the books so FPL General is here to preview gameweek 25 with a tight turnaround to Saturday's 11am deadline. All the usual wisdom plus these questions answered:</p><ul><li>Is it worth buying Bruno for the DGW or going straight to Salah?</li><li>Thoughts on bench boost in GW26 over TC Salah?</li><li>Is this a good time to wildcard without having Salah and a few players I’m not happy with?</li><li>What’s the plan to bring Salah back if I have KDB and Bruno?</li><li>Weghorst or Cornet to target for Burnley's double double?</li><li>Is Antonio to Weghorst the best move?</li><li>Should we replace Foden with Coutinho and is Dalot a good option going forward as a 5th defender?</li><li>What do you think about Raphinha, Watkins &amp; Antonio?</li><li>Which five players should we be targeting for DGW26?</li><li>Edouard benched again. Should we admit we got it wrong and cut our losses? Or hold for the good run fixtures and have faith that he’ll return?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></itunes:summary>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Gameweek 24 midweek fixtures preview</title>
			<itunes:title>Gameweek 24 midweek fixtures preview</itunes:title>
			<pubDate>Mon, 07 Feb 2022 18:20:00 GMT</pubDate>
			<itunes:duration>36:39</itunes:duration>
			<enclosure url="https://sphinx.acast.com/p/open/s/683750c96e5b65d787575771/e/83dd5f9e-8046-11ec-a255-a7e6dd853388/media.mp3" length="52836814" type="audio/mpeg"/>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">83dd5f9e-8046-11ec-a255-a7e6dd853388</guid>
			<itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
			<link>https://shows.acast.com/the-athletic-fpl-podcast/episodes/683750e2998551779fb871c2</link>
			<acast:episodeId>683750e2998551779fb871c2</acast:episodeId>
			<acast:showId>683750c96e5b65d787575771</acast:showId>
			<acast:settings><![CDATA[]]></acast:settings>
			<itunes:subtitle>FPL General is back after a lengthy gameweek 23 finally drew to a close at the weekend, and it was a tough one for a lot of managers. We look ahead to gameweek 24 with the usual array of transfer advice, watchlist updates, and your questions answered:</itunes:subtitle>
			<itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
			<itunes:image href="https://assets.pippa.io/shows/683750c96e5b65d787575771/show-cover.jpg"/>
			<description><![CDATA[FPL General is back after a lengthy gameweek 23 finally drew to a close at the weekend, and it was a tough one for a lot of managers. We look ahead to gameweek 24 with the usual array of transfer advice, watchlist updates, and these questions answered:</p><ul><li>What strategy would you go for with ALL CHIPS left to use?</li><li>How many hits is it worth taking for a Bench Boost, -4 or -8?</li><li>What do you think of Free Hit GW26 and have at least a strong 11 who all double, as opposed to the crowd of Triple Captain Salah as a part of a chip strategy?</li><li>Bruno. Salah. KdB. Ronaldo. Kane. Son. Which two or three do you see as the most effective from GWs 24-27?</li><li>With so many premium assets back in form, is it "essential", especially structure-wise, to have a two premium set up, or is it still viable to perma captain Salah and spread the cash?</li><li>Top 3 defenders to buy ahead of GW24 excluding Trent &amp; Cancelo? Unlimited budget.</li><li>Is Rashford a viable alternative to Ronaldo and Bruno as a Man United attacking option for the next two gameweeks?</li><li>Are the Crystal Palace options worth a punt? Good recent underlying stats but mostly from home games…next 3 out of 4 fixtures are away…</li><li>Is it worth holding the Watford strikers for the upcoming DGW?</li><li>Is it worth thinking outside the box when looking for strikers? Benteke, Edouard, Richarlison for example?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></description>
			<itunes:summary><![CDATA[FPL General is back after a lengthy gameweek 23 finally drew to a close at the weekend, and it was a tough one for a lot of managers. We look ahead to gameweek 24 with the usual array of transfer advice, watchlist updates, and these questions answered:</p><ul><li>What strategy would you go for with ALL CHIPS left to use?</li><li>How many hits is it worth taking for a Bench Boost, -4 or -8?</li><li>What do you think of Free Hit GW26 and have at least a strong 11 who all double, as opposed to the crowd of Triple Captain Salah as a part of a chip strategy?</li><li>Bruno. Salah. KdB. Ronaldo. Kane. Son. Which two or three do you see as the most effective from GWs 24-27?</li><li>With so many premium assets back in form, is it "essential", especially structure-wise, to have a two premium set up, or is it still viable to perma captain Salah and spread the cash?</li><li>Top 3 defenders to buy ahead of GW24 excluding Trent &amp; Cancelo? Unlimited budget.</li><li>Is Rashford a viable alternative to Ronaldo and Bruno as a Man United attacking option for the next two gameweeks?</li><li>Are the Crystal Palace options worth a punt? Good recent underlying stats but mostly from home games…next 3 out of 4 fixtures are away…</li><li>Is it worth holding the Watford strikers for the upcoming DGW?</li><li>Is it worth thinking outside the box when looking for strikers? Benteke, Edouard, Richarlison for example?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></itunes:summary>
		</item>
