		<item>
			<title>Should we be free hitting for the upcoming double gameweek?</title>
			<itunes:title>Should we be free hitting for the upcoming double gameweek?</itunes:title>
			<pubDate>Tue, 11 Jan 2022 14:12:00 GMT</pubDate>
			<itunes:duration>31:02</itunes:duration>
			<enclosure url="https://sphinx.acast.com/p/open/s/683750c96e5b65d787575771/e/db53c2a4-6af7-11ec-8fc5-d7efcaa6e127/media.mp3" length="44731611" type="audio/mpeg"/>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">db53c2a4-6af7-11ec-8fc5-d7efcaa6e127</guid>
			<itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
			<link>https://theathletic.com/podcast/166-fpl-podcast/?episode=90</link>
			<acast:episodeId>683750eb998551779fb8758b</acast:episodeId>
			<acast:showId>683750c96e5b65d787575771</acast:showId>
			<acast:settings><![CDATA[]]></acast:settings>
			<itunes:subtitle><![CDATA[The FPL General is back after the FA Cup break and ready to hit the ground running for the double gameweeks that lie ahead. There's all the usual transfer and captaincy talk, plus a watchlist update and his take on whether you need to use a free hit for the upcoming double gameweek]]></itunes:subtitle>
			<itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
			<itunes:image href="https://assets.pippa.io/shows/683750c96e5b65d787575771/show-cover.jpg"/>
			<description><![CDATA[The FPL General is back after the FA Cup break and ready to hit the ground running for the double gameweeks that lie ahead. There's all the usual transfer and captaincy talk, plus a watchlist update and these questions answered:</p><ul><li>With Son out injured and Salah at AFCON, is it worth free hitting for the double gameweek coming up? Or should we save both FHs for later?</li><li>Is it mad to use the 2nd WC this week?</li><li>I'll be hitting the Wildcard this GW. What are some must have pics for the double that I will want to keep long term?</li><li>Do you think it's prudent to withhold from using any chips until things settle down?</li><li>Best Son replacements? <strong> </strong></li><li>Should we be looking at Wolves defenders and if so which one is your preference?</li><li>Given all the uncertainty I’m thinking of keeping Salah to save transferring him back. Views? </li><li>If I have Salah &amp; Son, should I hold Salah &amp; use Son for replacements?</li><li>Is Dalot worth keeping? </li><li>Do we still keep Foden or sell?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></description>
			<itunes:summary><![CDATA[The FPL General is back after the FA Cup break and ready to hit the ground running for the double gameweeks that lie ahead. There's all the usual transfer and captaincy talk, plus a watchlist update and these questions answered:</p><ul><li>With Son out injured and Salah at AFCON, is it worth free hitting for the double gameweek coming up? Or should we save both FHs for later?</li><li>Is it mad to use the 2nd WC this week?</li><li>I'll be hitting the Wildcard this GW. What are some must have pics for the double that I will want to keep long term?</li><li>Do you think it's prudent to withhold from using any chips until things settle down?</li><li>Best Son replacements? <strong> </strong></li><li>Should we be looking at Wolves defenders and if so which one is your preference?</li><li>Given all the uncertainty I’m thinking of keeping Salah to save transferring him back. Views? </li><li>If I have Salah &amp; Son, should I hold Salah &amp; use Son for replacements?</li><li>Is Dalot worth keeping? </li><li>Do we still keep Foden or sell?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></itunes:summary>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Interviewing the elite managers: FPL Heisenberg</title>
			<itunes:title>Interviewing the elite managers: FPL Heisenberg</itunes:title>
			<pubDate>Thu, 06 Jan 2022 12:35:00 GMT</pubDate>
			<itunes:duration>50:15</itunes:duration>
			<enclosure url="https://sphinx.acast.com/p/open/s/683750c96e5b65d787575771/e/db15f244-6af7-11ec-8fc5-f32dd8669abf/media.mp3" length="72410710" type="audio/mpeg"/>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">db15f244-6af7-11ec-8fc5-f32dd8669abf</guid>
			<itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
			<link>https://shows.acast.com/the-athletic-fpl-podcast/episodes/683750ec9bd0275f2c4a45e6</link>
			<acast:episodeId>683750ec9bd0275f2c4a45e6</acast:episodeId>
			<acast:showId>683750c96e5b65d787575771</acast:showId>
			<acast:settings><![CDATA[]]></acast:settings>
			<itunes:subtitle>In the first of a series of interviews with the best FPL managers in the world, The General talks strategy with a member of the elite - FPL Heisenberg.</itunes:subtitle>
			<itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
			<itunes:image href="https://assets.pippa.io/shows/683750c96e5b65d787575771/show-cover.jpg"/>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>In the first of a series of interviews with the best FPL managers in the world, The General talks strategy with a member of the elite - FPL Heisenberg.</p><p>With multiple top 10K finishes under his belt, including a best ever of 836th in the world, FPL Heisenberg shares his philosophy on transfer strategy, whether he feels stats or the "eye test" yields more FPL success, and which stats and tools to look out for when looking for future FPL prospects.</p><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></description>
			<itunes:summary><![CDATA[<p>In the first of a series of interviews with the best FPL managers in the world, The General talks strategy with a member of the elite - FPL Heisenberg.</p><p>With multiple top 10K finishes under his belt, including a best ever of 836th in the world, FPL Heisenberg shares his philosophy on transfer strategy, whether he feels stats or the "eye test" yields more FPL success, and which stats and tools to look out for when looking for future FPL prospects.</p><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></itunes:summary>
