		<item>
			<title>Do we go for the Chelsea triple defence plus Trent and Cancelo?</title>
			<itunes:title>Do we go for the Chelsea triple defence plus Trent and Cancelo?</itunes:title>
			<pubDate>Tue, 23 Nov 2021 17:08:00 GMT</pubDate>
			<itunes:duration>33:21</itunes:duration>
			<enclosure url="https://sphinx.acast.com/p/open/s/683750c96e5b65d787575771/e/ed9bdbc8-3815-11ec-abc7-6797cfdb9cdb/media.mp3" length="48078416" type="audio/mpeg"/>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">ed9bdbc8-3815-11ec-abc7-6797cfdb9cdb</guid>
			<itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
			<link>https://theathletic.com/podcast/166-fpl-podcast/?episode=80</link>
			<acast:episodeId>683750de998551779fb870fb</acast:episodeId>
			<acast:showId>683750c96e5b65d787575771</acast:showId>
			<acast:settings><![CDATA[]]></acast:settings>
			<itunes:subtitle><![CDATA[With an action-packed gameweek 12 in the books the FPL General is here to assess the damage and get you ready to go again at the weekend. He's got a watchlist update, transfer and captaincy advice, plus his take on whether it's time to plough all our resources into defence.]]></itunes:subtitle>
			<itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
			<itunes:image href="https://assets.pippa.io/shows/683750c96e5b65d787575771/show-cover.jpg"/>
			<description><![CDATA[With an action-packed gameweek 12 in the books the FPL General is here to assess the damage and get you ready to go again at the weekend. He's got a watchlist update, transfer and captaincy advice, plus answers to these questions:</p><ul><li>If 5 at the back is a genuine option, can we say the Chelsea defensive triple is viable, along with Trent and Cancelo?</li><li> Is Dias to Chilwell a good transfer?</li><li> Antonio has 23 points from his last 9 gameweeks. What striker do we go for now?</li><li> Best under 6.5 forwards? Is Dennis the obvious choice?</li><li>Should we trust the fixtures and keep Vardy or just sell him because he is a 2 pts player too frequently recently?</li><li>How essential are Son and Kane when we could double up on the Chelsea wing backs for half the price instead?</li><li>Are there any decent replacements for Mbeumo around the same price?</li><li>Is Raphinha a hold? Or time to move to Jota if he’s fit?</li><li>Can we now start to look at Bernardo Silva as a legitimate option?</li><li>Is it wise to take an 8 or 12 point hit to steady the ship if my team is a mess, wildcard is played and I'm way down the rankings?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></description>
			<itunes:summary><![CDATA[With an action-packed gameweek 12 in the books the FPL General is here to assess the damage and get you ready to go again at the weekend. He's got a watchlist update, transfer and captaincy advice, plus answers to these questions:</p><ul><li>If 5 at the back is a genuine option, can we say the Chelsea defensive triple is viable, along with Trent and Cancelo?</li><li> Is Dias to Chilwell a good transfer?</li><li> Antonio has 23 points from his last 9 gameweeks. What striker do we go for now?</li><li> Best under 6.5 forwards? Is Dennis the obvious choice?</li><li>Should we trust the fixtures and keep Vardy or just sell him because he is a 2 pts player too frequently recently?</li><li>How essential are Son and Kane when we could double up on the Chelsea wing backs for half the price instead?</li><li>Are there any decent replacements for Mbeumo around the same price?</li><li>Is Raphinha a hold? Or time to move to Jota if he’s fit?</li><li>Can we now start to look at Bernardo Silva as a legitimate option?</li><li>Is it wise to take an 8 or 12 point hit to steady the ship if my team is a mess, wildcard is played and I'm way down the rankings?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></itunes:summary>
