		<item>
			<title>Lukaku - stick or twist?</title>
			<itunes:title>Lukaku - stick or twist?</itunes:title>
			<pubDate>Tue, 19 Oct 2021 13:07:00 GMT</pubDate>
			<itunes:duration>27:33</itunes:duration>
			<enclosure url="https://sphinx.acast.com/p/open/s/683750c96e5b65d787575771/e/3acdd1d8-2481-11ec-8983-eb577a63beb6/media.mp3" length="39717666" type="audio/mpeg"/>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">3acdd1d8-2481-11ec-8983-eb577a63beb6</guid>
			<itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
			<link>https://shows.acast.com/the-athletic-fpl-podcast/episodes/683750e19bd0275f2c4a4061</link>
			<acast:episodeId>683750e19bd0275f2c4a4061</acast:episodeId>
			<acast:showId>683750c96e5b65d787575771</acast:showId>
			<acast:settings><![CDATA[]]></acast:settings>
			<itunes:subtitle><![CDATA[The FPL General looks ahead to gameweek 9, fresh off the back of picking up a green arrow in GW8. He's got an updated watch list, transfer advice, captaincy picks and his take on whether to stick or twist with the underperforming Lukaku.]]></itunes:subtitle>
			<itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
			<itunes:image href="https://assets.pippa.io/shows/683750c96e5b65d787575771/show-cover.jpg"/>
			<description><![CDATA[The FPL General looks ahead to gameweek 9, fresh off the back of picking up a green arrow in GW8. He's got an updated watch list, transfer advice, captaincy picks and these questions answered:</p><ul><li>Lukaku. Stick or twist?!</li><li>Do I do Ronaldo to Lukaku or to Vardy?</li><li>Do we need to get Son now, or wait until his fixtures get better?</li><li>When (if at all) do we jump to Kane? Ron and Rom not really doing it</li><li>Is it time to start jumping off the West Ham assets?</li><li>Brought in Dias and Christensen on the wildcard, with *mixed* results. Are either of them a hold for this week?</li><li>I fear Greenwood will unfairly become Ole’s fall guy for United’s unbalanced team - hold on to him or switch now to avoid rotation risk?</li><li>Is it worth a punt on Werner?</li><li>I would consider Ings as unjustifiably underrated. His numbers compared to his price are great. Fixtures are ok. What am I missing? </li><li>Thoughts on triple Brentford?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></description>
			<itunes:summary><![CDATA[The FPL General looks ahead to gameweek 9, fresh off the back of picking up a green arrow in GW8. He's got an updated watch list, transfer advice, captaincy picks and these questions answered:</p><ul><li>Lukaku. Stick or twist?!</li><li>Do I do Ronaldo to Lukaku or to Vardy?</li><li>Do we need to get Son now, or wait until his fixtures get better?</li><li>When (if at all) do we jump to Kane? Ron and Rom not really doing it</li><li>Is it time to start jumping off the West Ham assets?</li><li>Brought in Dias and Christensen on the wildcard, with *mixed* results. Are either of them a hold for this week?</li><li>I fear Greenwood will unfairly become Ole’s fall guy for United’s unbalanced team - hold on to him or switch now to avoid rotation risk?</li><li>Is it worth a punt on Werner?</li><li>I would consider Ings as unjustifiably underrated. His numbers compared to his price are great. Fixtures are ok. What am I missing? </li><li>Thoughts on triple Brentford?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></itunes:summary>
