			<acast:episodeId>683750ed6e5b65d7875794c7</acast:episodeId>
			<acast:showId>683750c96e5b65d787575771</acast:showId>
			<acast:settings><![CDATA[]]></acast:settings>
			<itunes:subtitle><![CDATA[The FPL General reviews a disappointing gameweek for Ronaldo, Bruno Fernandes and Lukaku owners and looks ahead with renewed optimism to gameweek 6. There's the usual take on captaincy picks, transfer advice and a watchlist update]]></itunes:subtitle>
			<itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
			<itunes:image href="https://assets.pippa.io/shows/683750c96e5b65d787575771/show-cover.jpg"/>
			<description><![CDATA[The FPL General reviews a disappointing gameweek for Ronaldo, Bruno Fernandes and Lukaku owners and looks ahead with renewed optimism to gameweek 6. There's the usual take on captaincy picks, transfer advice, a watchlist update, plus these questions answered:</p><ul><li>Double Chelsea defence or 1 Chelsea and 1 City for next 5 GWs?</li><li>If you would wildcard this gameweek, what would your team be like?</li><li>Reasons to wait until gw8 for wc and not this week?</li><li>Is a missing / misfiring Chelsea midfield going to damage Lukaku's points potential?</li><li>Would you stick with Sanchez or go for Ramsdale assuming he is first choice now?</li><li>Is Saka a viable option over Sarr, looking at Watford's tougher fixtures and Arsenal's form turnaround?</li><li>What are your thoughts on Aston Villa defenders?</li><li>Do you feel comfortable going with Gallagher to fit in Ronaldo and Lukaku?</li><li>If you owned both Jota and Greenwood, which one would you be looking to move on first and is GW7 to right time to sell?</li><li>Best one week punt (any position, any price) before GW8 wildcard?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></description>
			<itunes:summary><![CDATA[The FPL General reviews a disappointing gameweek for Ronaldo, Bruno Fernandes and Lukaku owners and looks ahead with renewed optimism to gameweek 6. There's the usual take on captaincy picks, transfer advice, a watchlist update, plus these questions answered:</p><ul><li>Double Chelsea defence or 1 Chelsea and 1 City for next 5 GWs?</li><li>If you would wildcard this gameweek, what would your team be like?</li><li>Reasons to wait until gw8 for wc and not this week?</li><li>Is a missing / misfiring Chelsea midfield going to damage Lukaku's points potential?</li><li>Would you stick with Sanchez or go for Ramsdale assuming he is first choice now?</li><li>Is Saka a viable option over Sarr, looking at Watford's tougher fixtures and Arsenal's form turnaround?</li><li>What are your thoughts on Aston Villa defenders?</li><li>Do you feel comfortable going with Gallagher to fit in Ronaldo and Lukaku?</li><li>If you owned both Jota and Greenwood, which one would you be looking to move on first and is GW7 to right time to sell?</li><li>Best one week punt (any position, any price) before GW8 wildcard?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></itunes:summary>
