		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[The FPL General's Golden Rules + his latest GW1 draft]]></title>
			<itunes:title><![CDATA[The FPL General's Golden Rules + his latest GW1 draft]]></itunes:title>
			<pubDate>Tue, 10 Aug 2021 17:03:00 GMT</pubDate>
			<itunes:duration>41:04</itunes:duration>
			<enclosure url="https://sphinx.acast.com/p/open/s/683750c96e5b65d787575771/e/12a7581c-f3f0-11eb-9abf-c77c7f31c274/media.mp3" length="59178348" type="audio/mpeg"/>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">12a7581c-f3f0-11eb-9abf-c77c7f31c274</guid>
			<itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
			<link>https://shows.acast.com/the-athletic-fpl-podcast/episodes/683750f02780b226c7c00e04</link>
			<acast:episodeId>683750f02780b226c7c00e04</acast:episodeId>
			<acast:showId>683750c96e5b65d787575771</acast:showId>
			<acast:settings><![CDATA[]]></acast:settings>
			<itunes:subtitle><![CDATA[The FPL General's Golden Rules + his latest GW1 draft]]></itunes:subtitle>
			<itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
			<itunes:image href="https://assets.pippa.io/shows/683750c96e5b65d787575771/show-cover.jpg"/>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>With just a matter of days to go until the first FPL deadline of the season the FPL General is here with his all important golden rules to make sure you stay on track for a good season, he also takes you through his thoughts on captaincy choices for the first six gameweeks, and there's his all important first gameweek draft...</p><p>All that plus these listener questions asked:</p><ul><li>With emerging £4.0m defenders like Tsimikas and Amartey who could offer the same points as the big hitting defenders in the first few weeks, is it wise to go for cheap defenders and big on mids and forwards?</li><li>How important is a strong bench? </li><li>Why is Ings still an attractive asset?</li><li>Do you think a downgrade from Bruno to Sancho would be worth it to fit in Lukaku?</li><li>Can we go without Raphinha for the first 4? </li><li>What do you think about the Everton defence and especially Lucas Digne, is he worth £5.5m for the start of the season? </li><li>Would you be happy with Sanchez/Bachmann or a 4.5 keeper, or would you stretch to a 5/5.5 keeper?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></description>
			<itunes:summary><![CDATA[<p>With just a matter of days to go until the first FPL deadline of the season the FPL General is here with his all important golden rules to make sure you stay on track for a good season, he also takes you through his thoughts on captaincy choices for the first six gameweeks, and there's his all important first gameweek draft...</p><p>All that plus these listener questions asked:</p><ul><li>With emerging £4.0m defenders like Tsimikas and Amartey who could offer the same points as the big hitting defenders in the first few weeks, is it wise to go for cheap defenders and big on mids and forwards?</li><li>How important is a strong bench? </li><li>Why is Ings still an attractive asset?</li><li>Do you think a downgrade from Bruno to Sancho would be worth it to fit in Lukaku?</li><li>Can we go without Raphinha for the first 4? </li><li>What do you think about the Everton defence and especially Lucas Digne, is he worth £5.5m for the start of the season? </li><li>Would you be happy with Sanchez/Bachmann or a 4.5 keeper, or would you stretch to a 5/5.5 keeper?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></itunes:summary>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Ten tips for FPL success this season</title>
			<itunes:title>Ten tips for FPL success this season</itunes:title>
			<pubDate>Tue, 03 Aug 2021 17:33:00 GMT</pubDate>
			<itunes:duration>42:28</itunes:duration>
			<enclosure url="https://sphinx.acast.com/p/open/s/683750c96e5b65d787575771/e/12977762-f3f0-11eb-9abf-1390494e8f95/media.mp3" length="61200529" type="audio/mpeg"/>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">12977762-f3f0-11eb-9abf-1390494e8f95</guid>
			<itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
			<link>https://theathletic.com/podcast/166-fpl-podcast/?episode=57</link>
			<acast:episodeId>683750f56e5b65d7875796f8</acast:episodeId>
			<acast:showId>683750c96e5b65d787575771</acast:showId>
			<acast:settings><![CDATA[]]></acast:settings>
			<itunes:subtitle><![CDATA[New name, same essential wisdom from the FPL General - he's back with 11 days to go before the first deadline of the season with ten tips for success this season,]]></itunes:subtitle>
			<itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
			<itunes:image href="https://assets.pippa.io/shows/683750c96e5b65d787575771/show-cover.jpg"/>
			<description><![CDATA[New name, same FPL General - he's back with 11 days to go before the first deadline of the season with ten tips for success this season, plus the usual selection of burning questions from our listeners:</p><ul><li>Is it worth starting with a Chelsea and a City player so that you don't need to book transfers in early doors?</li><li>How will you consider Kane for GW2 at home to Norwich if he moves to and trains with Man City before the GW1 deadline?</li><li>As no player is "essential", how "necessary" is Bruno?</li><li>Raphinha aside, who would you have if the season started tomorrow?</li><li>Is<strong> </strong>Smith-Rowe a viable enabler or a transfer waiting to happen?</li><li>Is 4 at the back a viable strategy?</li><li>How many non-playing bench players would you advise for the start of the season?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></description>
			<itunes:summary><![CDATA[New name, same FPL General - he's back with 11 days to go before the first deadline of the season with ten tips for success this season, plus the usual selection of burning questions from our listeners:</p><ul><li>Is it worth starting with a Chelsea and a City player so that you don't need to book transfers in early doors?</li><li>How will you consider Kane for GW2 at home to Norwich if he moves to and trains with Man City before the GW1 deadline?</li><li>As no player is "essential", how "necessary" is Bruno?</li><li>Raphinha aside, who would you have if the season started tomorrow?</li><li>Is<strong> </strong>Smith-Rowe a viable enabler or a transfer waiting to happen?</li><li>Is 4 at the back a viable strategy?</li><li>How many non-playing bench players would you advise for the start of the season?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></itunes:summary>
