			<guid isPermaLink="false">5c50d010-624b-11eb-b2fc-6bbad51ed0e3</guid>
			<itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
			<link>https://theathletic.com/podcast/166-the-59th-minute-fpl-podcast/?episode=49</link>
			<acast:episodeId>683750ee9bd0275f2c4a463f</acast:episodeId>
			<acast:showId>683750c96e5b65d787575771</acast:showId>
			<acast:settings><![CDATA[]]></acast:settings>
			<itunes:subtitle>The General maintains hope of salvaging his FPL season with sage advice ahead of GW32 and beyond...</itunes:subtitle>
			<itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
			<itunes:image href="https://assets.pippa.io/shows/683750c96e5b65d787575771/show-cover.jpg"/>
			<description><![CDATA[The General is back to preview an extended gameweek 32, still haunted by wildcard sales of the recent past, as Jesse Lingard becomes officially impossible to ignore and Kai Havertz starts to show his class at Chelsea... Mark reveals his plan to break into the top 10k by the end of the season... And of course, answers to the following:</p><ul><li>Is Kane a good triple captain option for this week &amp; Is Son essential for the Spurs double?</li><li>Is it worth bringing in Iheanacho before his FA Cup tie?</li><li>Were the last couple of Chelsea matches just defensive blips?</li><li>Is Edinson Cavani worth it?</li><li>Emi Martinez over Edouard Mendy?</li><li>How best to use your free hit if you still have one?</li><li>And, will The General revert to a more conservative strategy from now until the end of the season after breaking some of his own golden rules?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></description>
			<itunes:summary><![CDATA[The General is back to preview an extended gameweek 32, still haunted by wildcard sales of the recent past, as Jesse Lingard becomes officially impossible to ignore and Kai Havertz starts to show his class at Chelsea... Mark reveals his plan to break into the top 10k by the end of the season... And of course, answers to the following:</p><ul><li>Is Kane a good triple captain option for this week &amp; Is Son essential for the Spurs double?</li><li>Is it worth bringing in Iheanacho before his FA Cup tie?</li><li>Were the last couple of Chelsea matches just defensive blips?</li><li>Is Edinson Cavani worth it?</li><li>Emi Martinez over Edouard Mendy?</li><li>How best to use your free hit if you still have one?</li><li>And, will The General revert to a more conservative strategy from now until the end of the season after breaking some of his own golden rules?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></itunes:summary>
