		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[Messi Lingard & Wildcard Advice for Gameweek 31]]></title>
			<itunes:title><![CDATA[Messi Lingard & Wildcard Advice for Gameweek 31]]></itunes:title>
			<pubDate>Tue, 06 Apr 2021 17:30:00 GMT</pubDate>
			<itunes:duration>33:54</itunes:duration>
			<enclosure url="https://sphinx.acast.com/p/open/s/683750c96e5b65d787575771/e/5c4d2672-624b-11eb-b2fc-7fed91b823e1/media.mp3" length="48880065" type="audio/mpeg"/>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">5c4d2672-624b-11eb-b2fc-7fed91b823e1</guid>
			<itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
			<link>https://theathletic.com/podcast/166-the-59th-minute-fpl-podcast/?episode=48</link>
			<acast:episodeId>683750f57b483718e05ed565</acast:episodeId>
			<acast:showId>683750c96e5b65d787575771</acast:showId>
			<acast:settings><![CDATA[]]></acast:settings>
			<itunes:subtitle><![CDATA[The FPL General may have played his wildcard earlier than planned but has no regrets and plenty of good advice ahead of Gameweek 31, with Trent Alexander-Arnold and Liverpool's resurgence catching the eye among others...]]></itunes:subtitle>
			<itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
			<itunes:image href="https://assets.pippa.io/shows/683750c96e5b65d787575771/show-cover.jpg"/>
			<description><![CDATA[The General is in a defiant mood after triggering his wildcard early but still has some sage advice for those of you who've patiently waited for Gameweek 31 to play it. A Liverpool revival continues to entice, as does the form of West Ham's Jesse Lingard, plus a totally re-imagined watchlist and answers to the following:</p><ul><li>Is Kane a set-and-forget captain until the end of the season?</li><li>Any advice for GW31 Wildcarders?</li><li>KDB, Fernandes, Salah &amp; Kane - Drop one!</li><li>How many Liverpool players do we need after their performance against Arsenal?</li><li>Is Ederson the safest defensive Man City pick?</li><li>Can we trust either Wolves or Arsenal defenders?</li><li>Who is the best differential wildcard DF, MF and FW option?</li><li>Marcos Alonso - stick or twist given recent game time?</li><li>And how do you feel about Iheanacho now?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></description>
			<itunes:summary><![CDATA[The General is in a defiant mood after triggering his wildcard early but still has some sage advice for those of you who've patiently waited for Gameweek 31 to play it. A Liverpool revival continues to entice, as does the form of West Ham's Jesse Lingard, plus a totally re-imagined watchlist and answers to the following:</p><ul><li>Is Kane a set-and-forget captain until the end of the season?</li><li>Any advice for GW31 Wildcarders?</li><li>KDB, Fernandes, Salah &amp; Kane - Drop one!</li><li>How many Liverpool players do we need after their performance against Arsenal?</li><li>Is Ederson the safest defensive Man City pick?</li><li>Can we trust either Wolves or Arsenal defenders?</li><li>Who is the best differential wildcard DF, MF and FW option?</li><li>Marcos Alonso - stick or twist given recent game time?</li><li>And how do you feel about Iheanacho now?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></itunes:summary>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[Gameweek 30 & The Wildcard 'Essentials']]></title>
			<itunes:title><![CDATA[Gameweek 30 & The Wildcard 'Essentials']]></itunes:title>
			<pubDate>Tue, 30 Mar 2021 15:30:00 GMT</pubDate>
			<itunes:duration>35:44</itunes:duration>
			<enclosure url="https://sphinx.acast.com/p/open/s/683750c96e5b65d787575771/e/5c49856c-624b-11eb-b2fc-bb42bff07caf/media.mp3" length="51536830" type="audio/mpeg"/>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">5c49856c-624b-11eb-b2fc-bb42bff07caf</guid>
			<itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
			<link>https://theathletic.com/podcast/166-the-59th-minute-fpl-podcast/?episode=47</link>
			<acast:episodeId>683750f3998551779fb87758</acast:episodeId>
			<acast:showId>683750c96e5b65d787575771</acast:showId>
			<acast:settings><![CDATA[]]></acast:settings>
			<itunes:subtitle>The General returns, refreshed, following the international break and ready to help you tackle the final 9 gameweeks of the season...</itunes:subtitle>
			<itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
			<itunes:image href="https://assets.pippa.io/shows/683750c96e5b65d787575771/show-cover.jpg"/>
			<description><![CDATA[Fantasy Premier League returns in Gameweek 30 with The General grateful to the international break for being able to enjoy a Sunday without any red arrows and to refocus on the final stretch... Why Arsenal's Martin Odegaard is a better player than an FPL player, a 'fling' with Marcos Alonso, as well as answers to the following:</p><ul><li>What to do with Man City assets now they *basically* have the Premier League all wrapped up?</li><li>Keep Bale and Son for Newcastle away?</li><li>Are Leeds' assets like Raphinha and Bamford worth keeping beyond GW30?</li><li>Who is the best one-week transfer if you plan on wildcarding in GW31?</li><li>Who are the best midfield options currently at £7.5m and under?</li><li>Pedro Neto's upcoming fixtures look good - is he worth a punt? </li><li>And, if you could have done one thing differently, what would it have been?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></description>
			<itunes:summary><![CDATA[Fantasy Premier League returns in Gameweek 30 with The General grateful to the international break for being able to enjoy a Sunday without any red arrows and to refocus on the final stretch... Why Arsenal's Martin Odegaard is a better player than an FPL player, a 'fling' with Marcos Alonso, as well as answers to the following:</p><ul><li>What to do with Man City assets now they *basically* have the Premier League all wrapped up?</li><li>Keep Bale and Son for Newcastle away?</li><li>Are Leeds' assets like Raphinha and Bamford worth keeping beyond GW30?</li><li>Who is the best one-week transfer if you plan on wildcarding in GW31?</li><li>Who are the best midfield options currently at £7.5m and under?</li><li>Pedro Neto's upcoming fixtures look good - is he worth a punt? </li><li>And, if you could have done one thing differently, what would it have been?</li></ul><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></itunes:summary>
