			<description><![CDATA[<p>With just the four fixtures for the FPL General to mull over as the dreaded blank Gameweek 29 approaches, he reveals why Arsenal left-back Kieran Tierney is a good option for the short <em>and </em>long-term... He also debates a one-week-punt on Leandro Trossard and whether "value-buy" Iheanacho will he make his wildcard squad?</p><p>Plus, answers to the following twitter questions:</p><ul><li>What is a reasonable amount of hits to take this week?</li><li>How do you handle multiple injuries in your squad?</li><li>Who are the top 5 players to target?</li><li>Is Lingard the best available Salah replacement for this GW?</li><li>Is it a good idea to play a wildcard during the international break?</li><li>Which differential players are you eyeing up?</li></ul><p>... And are Man City, Everton and Villa assets all now worth selling?</p><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></description>
