		<item>
			<title>How to tackle double gameweek 19 now that the fixtures have changed</title>
			<itunes:title>How to tackle double gameweek 19 now that the fixtures have changed</itunes:title>
			<pubDate>Thu, 14 Jan 2021 13:25:23 GMT</pubDate>
			<itunes:duration>27:41</itunes:duration>
			<enclosure url="https://sphinx.acast.com/p/open/s/683750c96e5b65d787575771/e/7a9f43c4-51a9-11eb-8159-07758c9b3051/media.mp3" length="39935463" type="audio/mpeg"/>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">7a9f43c4-51a9-11eb-8159-07758c9b3051</guid>
			<itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
			<link>https://theathletic.com/podcast/166-the-59th-minute-fpl-podcast/?episode=36</link>
			<acast:episodeId>683750ed7b483718e05ed35e</acast:episodeId>
			<acast:showId>683750c96e5b65d787575771</acast:showId>
			<acast:settings><![CDATA[]]></acast:settings>
			<itunes:subtitle>The FPL General is here to guide you through the ever-changing FPL landscape amidst yet more covid fixture chaos</itunes:subtitle>
			<itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
			<itunes:image href="https://assets.pippa.io/shows/683750c96e5b65d787575771/show-cover.jpg"/>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>The FPL General is here to guide you through the ever-changing FPL landscape amidst yet more covid fixture chaos, with all these questions about the massive double gameweek 19 answered:</p><ul><li>How many double GW players would you need to justify using the bench boost?</li><li>If you're not bench boosting in GW19 would triple captain be a good option instead?</li><li>Where do you draw the line at taking a points hit to make bench boost viable for the double GW?</li><li>Is a Manchester City defender now essential?</li><li>Is Michail Antonio worth a punt in the double gameweek?</li><li>Is Fernandes a risky captain now he's a yellow card away from missing a game in the double gameweek?</li><li>Would you still bench boost if you have three Leeds players, who only have a single game in GW19?</li><li>Is Salah a must-have for the double gameweek?</li><li>If we're not using bench boost this week when would be the next best opportunity?</li><li>Is not using bench boost or triple captain this week too risky?</li><li>Does the Villa double gameweek make their assets a stronger option given their run of good fixtures?</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Plus there's plenty of transfer &amp; captaincy advice and the usual watchlist in/out update</p><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></description>
			<itunes:summary><![CDATA[<p>The FPL General is here to guide you through the ever-changing FPL landscape amidst yet more covid fixture chaos, with all these questions about the massive double gameweek 19 answered:</p><ul><li>How many double GW players would you need to justify using the bench boost?</li><li>If you're not bench boosting in GW19 would triple captain be a good option instead?</li><li>Where do you draw the line at taking a points hit to make bench boost viable for the double GW?</li><li>Is a Manchester City defender now essential?</li><li>Is Michail Antonio worth a punt in the double gameweek?</li><li>Is Fernandes a risky captain now he's a yellow card away from missing a game in the double gameweek?</li><li>Would you still bench boost if you have three Leeds players, who only have a single game in GW19?</li><li>Is Salah a must-have for the double gameweek?</li><li>If we're not using bench boost this week when would be the next best opportunity?</li><li>Is not using bench boost or triple captain this week too risky?</li><li>Does the Villa double gameweek make their assets a stronger option given their run of good fixtures?</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Plus there's plenty of transfer &amp; captaincy advice and the usual watchlist in/out update</p><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></itunes:summary>
