			<description><![CDATA[<p>The FPL General drops his weekly dose of wisdom as we look ahead to gameweek 12 of the FPL season, including his thoughts on whether Mohammed Salah is the must-have captaincy option this week, plus his usual watchlist update, transfer advice and the following questions answered:</p><p>Is it worth dropping De Bruyne for Salah this week?</p><p>Who are your preferred sub 4.5 million defenders?</p><p>Would I be stupid to sell Ramsdale now after having him since GW1?</p><p>Is the goalscoring rate of Zouma and Vestergaard sustainable?</p><p>Is Son a must own at his current price?</p><p>Should we keep the faith in Jota or spend the cash on Trent instead?</p><p>Is it safe to go Bruno, KDB, Salah and Son in midfield?</p><p>Are Reece James and Chilwell the new Trent and Robertson?</p><p>How would you rank the premium assets through to GW15?</p><p>Who is a differential risk to target before a wilcard in GW16?</p><br><p>For this week's partnership go to www.virginwines.co.uk/theathletic</p><hr><p style='color:grey; font-size:0.75em;'> Hosted on Acast. See <a style='color:grey;' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' href='https://acast.com/privacy'>acast.com/privacy</a> for more information.</p>]]></description>
